    - row:
      - cell "Before the Iron: How Koreans Smoothed Clothes | Dadeumijil #KoreanCulture개 선택" [ref=e92]:
        - checkbox "Before the Iron: How Koreans Smoothed Clothes | Dadeumijil #KoreanCulture개 선택" [ref=e94]
      - cell:
        - link "동영상 미리보기 이미지: Before the Iron: How Koreans Smoothed Clothes | Dadeumijil #KoreanCulture 1:08" [ref=e95]
        - link "Before the Iron: How Koreans Smoothed Clothes | Dadeumijil #KoreanCulture" [ref=e96]
        - text: "Before electric irons, how did people make a garment smooth?\nTwo women beat cloth on a low stone in a Korean practice called dadeumijil. Washed and starched fabric was pounded to smooth its surface.\n\nFollow the wooden beaters and the different angles of their arms. This genre painting brings the often unseen work behind a clean white garment into view.\n\nCollection item: APKC260507306 · genre painting attributed to Uncho\nFrom the TJ Kim Collection\nMusic: Flow Music, \"종이 위의 바람\" (AI-generated music"
      - cell:
