        - link "Joseon's Board Game: Yutnori, Korea's Game of Sticks and Strategy #yutnori #KoreanCulture" [ref=e107]
        - text: "How did people in Joseon-era Korea spend a day off?\nFour people sit around a low board. Today's star is yutnori.\n\nInstead of dice, players throw four wooden sticks and move their pieces around the board, choosing routes and racing to bring every piece home. A lucky throw helps, but a smart choice matters too. Traditionally played around the Lunar New Year, the game brings families and neighbors together.\n\nFor 19th-century visitors to Korea, pictures like this were a window onto everyday life in"
